    <categoryEntry name="Psyker" id="e691-aad7-d21c-1023" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Psychic Powers" id="4e88-5913-b3b1-d3a0" hidden="false">
          <description>When you select a PSYKER unit to manifest psychic powers, you select one Psychic power that unit knows and attempt to manifest it. 
A PSYKER unit cannot attempt to manifest the same Psychic power more than once during the same battle round. 
Add 1 to the Warp charge value of the Psychic power for each other attempt that has been made to manifest that power by a unit from your army in this phase, whether that attempt was successful or not.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Transport" id="6cc4-1b62-8e8a-05cd" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Transport" id="5d83-b8a7-7066-3bfd" hidden="false">
          <description>- When a transport model is destroyed, check if it explodes*.
- Roll one D6 for each embarked model. If the transport has exploded, one model is removed for each roll of 1-4. If the transport has not exploded, one model is removed for each roll of 1-2.
- Disembark the remaining models wholly within 3&quot; of the transport model. If you cannot set up a model, it&apos;s considered to be destroyed.
- Units that disembarked cannot charge or perform Heroic Interventions this turn.

*If the transport doesn&apos;t have an Explodes rule or similar (which is considered as the Explodes in regard this Rule), consider as if the transport has not exploded in regard this Rule.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
