      <profiles>
        <profile name="Building Set-up" id="aa07-1c87-d0c4-20ba" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">- Units with Fortification Network battle-role can be set up within the Deployment Zone and more than 9&quot; of enemy units instead of wholly within the Deployment Zone.
- Each time you set up a unit with Fortification Network battle-role before the battle, you can select one Terrain Feature object in the battlefield that is within your deployment zone. You can remove that Terrain Feature.
- Units with Fortification Network battle-role cannot be set-up within 3&quot; of any Terrain Feature.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Unaligned" id="9df5-bb14-9326-4108" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Imperium" id="84e2-9fa9-ebe6-1d18" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Adeptus Astartes" id="c7b7-edbc-bc14-6238" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Combat Doctrines" id="332c-be53-25a0-23d2" hidden="true">
          <description>At the beggining of your Command Phase, if your Warlord is on the Battlefield, you can select a Combat Doctrine to take effect until your next Command Phase.
This Doctrines will affect all units which have the Faction: Adeptus Astartes Keyword present on the battlefield.
From the beggining of the first battle round until changed, the Devastator Doctrine is considered to be active.

1 - Devastator Doctrine: Whilst is active, models with this keyword do not suffer the penalty for moving and firing Heavy weapons, and when resolving an attack made with a Heavy weapon by a unit with this ability, you can re-roll one hit roll when resolving that weapon’s attacks.

2 - Tactical Doctrine: Whilst is active, models with this keyword do not suffer the penalty for advancing and firing Assault weapons, and when advanced, is possible to shoot with a Rapid-Fire or Pistol weapon, but must substract 1 from the hit roll.

3 - Assault Doctrine: Whilst is active, models with this keyword do not suffer the penalty for firing Heavy weapons in Engagement Range, and when resolving an attack made with a Pistol or Melee weapon by a unit with this ability, re-roll one hit roll for each model when resolving that unit’s attacks.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="CQB training" id="a5da-eee3-b550-3054" hidden="false">
          <description>When a unit from Faction: Adeptus Astartes fires Overwatch or Searching for Targets, it scores a hit on a unmodified roll of 5+.
If the unit has the INFANTRY Keyword and is in a DEFENSIBLE terrain feature, it scores a hit on a unmodified roll of 3+.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Astra Militarum" id="3263-4233-4344-6228" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Defence tactics" id="f555-0348-726b-7ee9" hidden="false">
          <description>When a INFANTRY unit from Faction: Astra Militarum fires Overwatch or Searching for Targets and is in a DEFENSIBLE terrain feature, it scores a hit on a unmodified roll of 4+.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
