    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Chaos Daemons" id="852c-3de9-a35c-01e6" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Daemonic Terror [Aura]" id="0abd-509b-4dce-9b05" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">While an enemy unit without INORGANIC, DAEMON or DAEMONIC Keywords is within 6&quot; of this unit, subtract 1 from that enemy unit’s Leadership characteristic and subtract 1 from any Combat Attrition tests taken for that enemy unit.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Manifestation" id="3de9-2035-5f0c-b7a8" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <comment>Not Infantry-Beast
Not Icon</comment>
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">During deployment, you can set up this unit in the warp instead of setting it up on the battlefield. If you do so, then in the Reinforcements step of one of your Movement phases you can set up this unit anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 6+D3&quot; away from any enemy models.
In addition, each time a unit with this ability makes a Morale test, on a roll of 1, one of it&apos;s models return to the battlefield with all of it&apos;s wounds remaining.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="7892-58f7-e769-4d87" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228" type="set" value="During deployment, you can set up this unit in the warp instead of setting it up on the battlefield. If you do so, then in the Reinforcements step of one of your Movement phases you can set up this unit anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 6+D3&quot; away from any enemy models.">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="ef18-746a-369f-43a4" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Manifestation" id="a24e-1c54-bdbd-8d26" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <comment>Infantry-Beast
Not Icon</comment>
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">During deployment, you can set up this unit in the warp instead of setting it up on the battlefield. If you do so, then in the Reinforcements step of one of your Movement phases you can set up this unit anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 6+D3&quot; away from any enemy models.
In addition, each time a unit with this ability makes a Morale test, on a roll of 1, up to 1D3 of it&apos;s models return to the battlefield with all of it&apos;s wounds remaining.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="7892-58f7-e769-4d87" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228" type="set" value="During deployment, you can set up this unit in the warp instead of setting it up on the battlefield. If you do so, then in the Reinforcements step of one of your Movement phases you can set up this unit anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 6+D3&quot; away from any enemy models.">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="ef18-746a-369f-43a4" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Warp Storm effects" id="2fe1-6781-805c-bd22" hidden="true">
          <description>At the start of each battle round, you can make a Warp Storm roll. 
To do so, roll up to nine D6. For each 4+, gain 1 Warp Storm point (WSP).
 - If your Warlord have the Mark of Nurgle, you can roll up to 7 D6.
 - If your Warlord have the Mark of Khorne, you can roll up to 8 D6.
 - If your Warlord have the Mark of Slaanesh, you can roll up to 6 D6, and can re-roll any of the dice.
Warp Storm points can be spent during that battle round on the Warp Storm effects.
You can always select effects from UNDIVIDED, and, if your Warlord has a dedicated Chaos Mark, you can also select Warp Storm effects from that Chaos allegiance.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Warp Storm effects,  Undivided" id="9851-4403-38aa-ba58" hidden="true">
          <description>UNDIVIDED---------------------------------------------
6WSP-----&gt;DARK INVIGORATION
Use this effect at the start of the Morale phase. One model in each FACTION: CHAOS DAEMONS unit from your army can regain up to D3 lost wounds. 
If every model in that unit has a Wounds characteristic of 1, that unit can instead be replenished. When a unit is replenished, you can return D3 destroyed models to that unit with their full wounds remaining.

3WSP-----&gt;MUSIC OF THE WARP
Use this effect at the start of your turn. Until the end of the turn, add 6&quot; to the range of the Daemonic Terror ability for INSTRUMENT units from your army (to a maximum of 12&quot;).

4WSP-----&gt;MAGNIFIED GLORY
Use this effect at the start of any turn. Until the end of the turn, add 3&quot; to the range of aura abilities of FACTION: CHAOS DAEMONS units from your army.

2WSP-----&gt;OTHERWORLDLY TREAD
Use this effect at the start of your Movement phase or at the start of your Charge phase. Until the end of the phase, FACTION: CHAOS DAEMONS units from your army can ignore any or all modifiers to their Move characteristic, Advance rolls and charge rolls.

4WSP-----&gt;DESCENDING SHADOW
Use this effect at the start of your opponent’s Shooting phase. Until the end of the phase, each time a ranged attack is made against a FACTION: CHAOS DAEMONS unit from your army, if the attacker is more than 12&quot; away, subtract 1 from that attack’s hit roll.

2WSP-----&gt;INSIDIOUS WHISPERS
Use this effect at the start of your opponent’s Psychic phase. Until the end of the phase, while an enemy PSYKER unit is within 12&quot; of a FACTION: CHAOS DAEMONS unit from your army, each time a Psychic test is taken for that PSYKER unit, it suffers Perils of the Warp on any dice roll that includes a double, instead of only a double 1 or double 6.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
