    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Adeptus Sororitas" id="f475-3e56-fd5f-4737" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Zealot" id="d056-70fc-2575-5b86" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Each time a model in this unit makes a melee attack, if this unit made a charge move, was charged or performed a Heroic Intervention this turn, you can re-roll that attack’s hit roll.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="c8fd-783f-3230-493e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Shield of Faith" id="069e-0ef4-b6c9-87c5" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">In your opponent’s Psychic phase, this unit can attempt to deny one psychic power as if it were a PSYKER. Each time a Deny the Witch test is taken for this unit, roll one D6 instead of 2D6: if the result of that test was an unmodified result of 6, or if it was greater than the result of the Psychic test, that Deny the Witch test is passed.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="c8fd-783f-3230-493e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Enduring will" id="a9fa-309a-ef88-a83c" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Each time a model with this ability would lose a wound, roll one D6: on a 6+, that wound is not lost.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Defence tactics" id="87d1-ae91-d7ea-1ce6" hidden="false">
          <description>When a unit from Faction: Adepta Sororitas fires Overwatch or Searching for Targets, it scores a hit on a unmodified roll of 5+.
If the unit has the INFANTRY Keyword and is in a DEFENSIBLE terrain feature, it scores a hit on a unmodified roll of 4+.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Acts of Faith" id="cc98-72d1-8072-cfee" hidden="true">
          <description>Once per phase, one unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith. To do so, you will use Miracle dice.

Gaining Miracle Dice:
 - At the start of each turn, you gain 1 Miracle dice.
 - At the end of a phase, when any Adepta Sororitas destroy one or more enemy units.
 - At the end of a phase, when one or more Adepta Sororitas Character units from your army are destroyed.

Each time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side - this is your Miracle dice pool.

Use of Miracle Dice:
Before making a dice roll for a model or a unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. 
To do so, select one or more of the dice from your Miracle dice pool, instead of making any or all of those dice rolls. 
For each individual dice that is being rolled as part of the dice roll, you can select 1 Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool to be substituted in place of that dice. 
The dice that it is being substituted for is not rolled, and instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled. 
Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once, and when used, removed from the Miracle dice pool.
A Miracle dice that has been used for a substitution can never be re-rolled.

You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:
- Advance roll
- Charge roll
- Hit roll
- Wound roll
- Saving throw
- Damage roll
- Morale test</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Sacred Rites" id="285a-e3f9-6af8-6972" hidden="true">
          <description>After players have determined their mission, you must select one sacred rite from the following table to be active for your army. 
Alternatively, you can randomly determine two sacred rites from the table to be active for your army by rolling two D6 and looking up the results.

1 - Hand of the Emperor: While this sacred rite is active, add 1 to Advance rolls and charge rolls made for this unit.

2 - Spirit of the Martyr: While this sacred rite is active, each time a model in this unit is destroyed by a melee attack and does not explode, roll one D6: on a 6, after the attacking model’s unit has finished making its attacks, it suffers 1 mortal wound.

3 - Aegis of the Emperor: While this sacred rite is active, each time this unit uses its Shield of Faith ability to take a Deny the Witch test, if the result of that test was an unmodified result of 5+, or if it was greater than the result of the Psychic test, that Deny the Witch test is passed.

4 - Divine Guidance: While this sacred rite is active, each time a model in this unit makes a ranged attack, on an unmodified wound roll of 6, the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack is improved by 1.

5 - The Passion: While this sacred rite is active, each time a model in this unit makes a melee attack, an unmodified hit roll of 6 scores 1 additional hit.

6 - Light of the Emperor: While this sacred rite is active, you can ignore any or all modifiers to this unit’s Leadership characteristic, and each time a Combat Attrition test is taken for this unit, you can ignore any or all modifiers.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Asuryani" id="1114-7875-d463-df17" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Martial training" id="5c5f-4783-ba47-6b80" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Each time a melee attack is made against a unit with this ability, a hit roll of 1-2 for that attack fails. 
Substract 1 from that attack&apos;s hit roll.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="1c6f-0311-3eba-3180" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Battle focus" id="3c90-6e36-ead1-2e94" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">ASURYANI INFANTRY and BIKER units this ability are eligible to shoot in a turn in which it Advanced, but if it does so, then until the end of the phase, models in this unit can only make attacks with Assault or Pistol weapons they are equipped with, and when resolving those attacks, that unit is treated as having Remained Stationary.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="1c6f-0311-3eba-3180" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Titanic Warlord" id="6c1d-32d6-b16c-3b0c" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Daemon Primarch" id="da67-195b-7909-341a" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Supreme Commander" id="5750-de0a-589d-eacf" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="S.C. Detachment" id="26b0-4bb9-73aa-d3d7" hidden="false">
      <comment>Supreme Command Detachment Unit</comment>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Core" id="08f1-d244-eb44-7e01" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Renegades and Heretics" id="f77e-c60e-d970-289a" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Adeptus Mechanicus" id="ca27-5069-1c2c-a28b" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Defence tactics" id="d32c-8cd9-9bb0-3598" hidden="false">
          <description>When a unit from Faction: Adeptus Mechanicus fires Overwatch or Searching for Targets, it scores a hit on a unmodified roll of 5+.
When a INFANTRY or INORGANIC BEAST unit from Faction: Adeptus Mechanicus fires Overwatch or Searching for Targets and is in a DEFENSIBLE terrain feature, it scores a hit on a unmodified roll of 4+.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Daemon Prince" id="d8d3-6bf7-9b21-8e58" hidden="false">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="2580-d1be-f19a-e54c" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="-1"/>
      </constraints>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="2580-d1be-f19a-e54c" type="set" value="1">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="cb2e-2f63-133e-a79c" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="greaterThan" value="0"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Be&apos;lakor" id="cb2e-2f63-133e-a79c" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Obstacle" id="7d4c-822b-b174-1e96" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Void Shield Generator" id="60c3-2c5d-0caa-e9ec" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Void Shield Generator" id="9f54-3f6c-86ac-0889" hidden="false">
          <description>- Each time a saving throw is failed for this model, if it has any Void Shield Layers, it does not suffer any damage. 
- Instead, for each point of damage inflicted, one of its Void Shield Layer loses 1 wound. Once a Void Shield Layer has lost a wound, it must continue to lose shield points due to any further damage inflicted until it collapses. 
- Each time an attack causes a Void Shield Layer to be reduced to 0 wounds, that Void Shield Layer collapses, and any excess damage inflicted by that attack is lost. 
- Void shields can never be used to prevent mortal wounds (each mortal wound inflicted on a model with void shields causes that model to lose one wound as normal).</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Inorganic" id="378d-72a9-b8f6-b98b" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Inorganic" id="ecb0-296d-22b0-35b5" hidden="false">
          <description>Units with the INORGANIC Keyword automaticly pass Morale tests.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Indirect fire" id="9f18-f587-3245-07e5" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Indirect fire" id="146a-976d-d046-6d66" hidden="false">
          <description>This weapon can target units that are not visible to the bearer. Substract 1 from the hit rolls against units that are not visible to the bearer&apos;s unit.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Wheeled" id="fd98-5ba2-04bf-821f" hidden="false">
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="[Action] Moving battlefield wrecks and debris." id="aaa8-162d-4fe1-2e4d" hidden="false" targetId="88ce-d161-bfbe-d554" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Wheeled" id="b280-3d33-92b5-c7d8" hidden="false">
          <description>- Models with this keyword can&apos;t move sideways.
- For simplicity reasons, when turning on the spot or in less than 1&quot;, each turn from 0º up to 45º without moving more than 1&quot; between turns, count as 1&quot; of movement, as each consecutive 45º turn from that point cost an additional 1&quot; of movement.
- Each time a unit with this keyword is selected to shoot, it can&apos;t turn to face the enemy unit, and the targeting of it&apos;s weapons are limited to the firing arc of the mounting point.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Tracked" id="7402-3477-84a2-08f8" hidden="false">
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="[Action] Moving battlefield wrecks and debris." id="a8c9-8678-59c6-30a7" hidden="false" targetId="88ce-d161-bfbe-d554" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Tracked" id="107c-1e23-4097-cf3f" hidden="false">
          <description>- Models with this keyword can&apos;t move sideways, but can turn on the spot.
- For simplicity reasons, when turning on the spot, each turn from 45º up to 90º without moving more than 1&quot; between turns, counts as 1&quot; of movement, as each consecutive 45º turn from that point cost an additional 1&quot; of movement.
- Each time a unit with this keyword is selected to shoot, it can turn to face the enemy unit up to 45º either side, and the targeting of it&apos;s weapons are limited to the firing arc of the mounting point.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Walker" id="27d8-f0bb-f3cc-580f" hidden="false">
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="[Action] Moving battlefield wrecks and debris." id="f73c-934c-a8c7-7b95" hidden="false" targetId="88ce-d161-bfbe-d554" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Walker" id="92da-da42-b805-8240" hidden="false">
          <description>- Models with this keyword can move sideways and turn on the spot.
- Each time a unit with this keyword is selected to shoot, before selecting targets, it can turn to face the enemy unit, and the targeting of it&apos;s weapons are limited to the firing arc of the mounting point.
- Arm-mounted weapons are considered to have 120º of firing arc, being up to 90º to the side where it&apos;s mounted.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Levitating" id="96e8-7e9d-42d7-2fea" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Levitating" id="d83e-928b-292c-a38f" hidden="false">
          <description>- Models with this keyword can move sideways and turn on the spot. 
- Models with this keyword are not affected by Difficult Terrain feature.
- Each time a unit with this keyword is selected to shoot, before selecting targets, it can turn to face the enemy unit, and the targeting of it&apos;s weapons are limited to the firing arc of the mounting point.
- This rule only take effect if the unit doesn&apos;t have active the Airborne ability.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Assault Transport" id="3c95-4bac-d4d4-d0b2" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Assault Transport" id="c10e-d1d4-14da-d564" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Units embarked within this TRANSPORT can disembark and either make a Normal move or Charge even if the TRANSPORT has Moved during this phase.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifierGroups>
            <modifierGroup type="and">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="d7c1-93c2-0c88-7c3c" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="name" type="set" value="Assault Transport (Ramp)">
                  <comment>Units embarked within this TRANSPORT can disembark and make a Normal move, Advance move and Charge even if the TRANSPORT has Moved during this phase.</comment>
                </modifier>
                <modifier field="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228" type="set" value="Units embarked within this TRANSPORT can disembark and make a Normal move, Advance move and Charge even if the TRANSPORT has Moved during this phase.">
                  <comment>Units embarked within this TRANSPORT can disembark and make a Normal move, Advance move and Charge even if the TRANSPORT has Moved during this phase.</comment>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </modifierGroup>
          </modifierGroups>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Bolt Weapon" id="fe8c-9fa3-c71e-d8de" hidden="true"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Bolt Weapon (Hvy)" id="b3c0-69fa-86d1-490c" hidden="true"/>
