  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Explodes 6+ (6&quot;)" id="3541-94a7-a138-358b" hidden="false">
      <description>When this model is destroyed, roll one D6 before any embarked models disembark and before removing it from play. On a 6 it explodes, and each unit within 6&quot; suffers D3 mortal wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Open-topped" id="60db-65f7-ca20-7874" hidden="false">
      <description>Models embarked on this model can attack in their Shooting phase. Measure the range and draw line of sight from any point on the model. When they do so, any restrictions or modifiers that apply to this model also apply to its passengers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord Traits" id="ce5a-0526-287b-4ff8" hidden="false">
      <description>If your Warlord is a CHARACTER, it can use a Warlord Trait. Immediately before either player starts to deploy their army, you can roll a D3 on the Warlord Trait table here to determine what Warlord Trait your Warlord has. Alternatively, choose the trait that most suits your Warlord&apos;s temperament or style of war.

1) Legendary Fighter: If this Warlord charges in the Charge phase, add 1 to their Attacks characteristic until the end of the ensuing Fight phase.

2) Inspiring Leader: Friendly units within 6&quot; of this Warlord can add 1 to their Leadership characteristic.

3) Tenacious Survivor: Roll a dice each time this Warlord loses a wound.  On a 6, the Warlord shrugs off the damage and does not lose the wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hateful Assault" id="73c3-c791-cd2f-6ad2" hidden="false">
      <description>If this unit makes a charge move, is charged or performs a Heroic Intervention, add 1 to the Attacks characteristic of models in this unit until the end of the turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Objective Secured" id="e07e-8dbf-0b15-7485" hidden="false" page="237">
      <comment>A player controls an objective marker if they have any models with this ability within range of that objective marker, even if the sum of remaining Wounds of the enemy models within the objective marker are larger than the sum of the friendly ones. 
If an enemy model within range of an objective marker also has this ability (or a similar ability), then the objective marker is controlled by the player who has the most Wounds remaining in models within range of that objective marker, as normal.</comment>
      <description>Units with this ability consider the Wounds characteristic of their models twice in regard Objective control.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Transport" id="55df-0779-8cb7-fa8b" hidden="false"/>
    <rule name="Explodes 6+ (3&quot;)" id="a90c-078f-b826-e2d4" hidden="false">
      <description>When this model is destroyed, roll one D6 before any embarked models disembark and before removing it from play. On a 6 it explodes, and each unit within 3&quot; suffers D3 mortal wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explodes 6+ (D6+3&quot;)" id="296c-b773-7bdb-fcf1" hidden="false">
      <description>When this model is destroyed, roll one D6 before any embarked models disembark and before removing it from play. On a 6 it explodes, and each unit within D6+3&quot; suffers D6 mortal wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explodes 6+ (D6+6&quot; / D6)" id="bd0f-186b-3ccc-e655" hidden="false">
      <description>When this model is destroyed, roll one D6 before any embarked models disembark and before removing it from play. On a 6 it explodes, and each unit within D6+6&quot; suffers 2D6 mortal wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Variable weapon profile" id="2dd5-c9f0-aa5a-818a" hidden="false">
      <description>Before selecting targets, select one of the aviable profiles to make attacks with.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Missile weapon profile" id="5ffa-b450-85d1-c3c7" hidden="false">
      <description>Before selecting targets, select between Flak, Frag or Krak missile weapon profiles to make attacks with.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Plasma weapon profile" id="6a90-8d3d-30d0-71b4" hidden="false">
      <description>Before selecting targets, select between Standard or Overcharge weapon profiles to make attacks with.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grenade weapon profile" id="4d69-d626-eb30-fe92" hidden="false">
      <description>Before selecting targets, select between Frag or Krak grenade weapon profiles to make attacks with.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Combined weapon" id="18d3-6068-7f55-0d0a" hidden="false">
      <description>When attacking with this weapon, choose one or both of the profiles. 
If you choose both, subtract 1 from all hit rolls for this weapon.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Authority of the Inquisition" id="ae43-91bd-1487-7974" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Warlord is a ORDO Character:
- All units in the Inquisitorial Army are affected by ORDO Keyword abilities as if it were a &lt;CHAPTER&gt;/&lt;REGIMENT&gt;/&lt;BROTHERHOOD&gt; Keyword.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Immobile" id="5a61-a53a-b4aa-0dd7" hidden="false">
      <description>This model cannot move for any reason, nor can it fight in the Fight phase. When resolving an attack made against this model in the Fight phase, do not make a hit roll: it automatically scores a hit. This model can shoot in your Shooting phase even if there are enemy models within 1&quot; of it, and friendly units can still target enemy units that are within 1&quot; of this model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explodes 4+ (D6+3&quot;)" id="d004-7f1d-1fff-43e2" hidden="false">
      <description>When this model is destroyed, roll one D6 before any embarked models disembark and before removing it from play. On a 6 it explodes, and each unit within D6+3&quot; suffers D6 mortal wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explodes 4+ (D6+6&quot; / D6)" id="2e1f-16eb-7f19-128f" hidden="false">
      <description>When this model is destroyed, roll one D6 before any embarked models disembark and before removing it from play. On a 6 it explodes, and each unit within D6+6&quot; suffers 2D6 mortal wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special-Issue Ammunition: Boltgun Ammo" id="b4aa-63ec-fd2e-978e" hidden="false">
      <description>Units with weapons with this ability can select their ammo before shooting with weapons with compatible ammo ability. 
By default, standard ammo will be shot (no changes to the weapon&apos;s profile).

- Metalstorm Frag Rounds: Do D3 attacks for each attack the weapon has. Reduce the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack to 0.
- Dragonfire Bolts: The target does not receive the benefits of cover against that attack.
- Hellfire Rounds: Add 1 to that attack’s wound roll against a unit that does not have the INORGANIC, VEHICLE or TITANIC keywords.
- Kraken Bolts: Add 6&quot; to the Range characteristic and improve the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack to -2.
- Vengeance Rounds: Add 1 to the Damage characteristic of that attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special-Issue Ammunition: Heavy Boltgun Ammo" id="dfdc-a0cc-daf0-a194" hidden="false">
      <description>Units with weapons with this ability can select their ammo before shooting with weapons with compatible ammo ability. 
By default, standard ammo will be shot (no changes to the weapon&apos;s profile).

- Shrapnel Bolts: Do D3 attacks for each attack the weapon has. Reduce the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack to 0.
- Hellfire Rounds: Add 1 to that attack’s wound roll against a unit that does not have the INORGANIC, VEHICLE or TITANIC keywords.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Icarus mount and tracking system" id="9ba0-cb9c-82a8-a8be" hidden="false">
      <description>Weapons with this rule ignore the Hard to hit ability.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wanton acts" id="f4d1-25d7-a7c7-4eea" hidden="false">
      <description>This Wanton Acts will affect all units which have the Faction: Chaotic Astartes Keyword present on the battlefield.
From the beggining of the first battle round until changed, the Wanton Destruction act is considered to be active.
A unit can be affected by only one Wanton act at a time.

1 - Wanton Destruction: Whilst is active, each time a model with this keyword makes an attack with a Heavy, Rapid Fire or Grenade weapon, an unmodified hit roll of 6 scores 1 additional hit.

2 - Wanton Massacre: Whilst is active, each time a model with this keyword makes an attack with a Rapid Fire, Assault or Pistol weapon, an unmodified hit roll of 6 scores 1 additional hit.

3 - Wanton Slaughter: Whilst is active, each time a model with this keyword makes an attack with an Assault, Pistol or melee weapon, an unmodified hit roll of 6 scores 1 additional hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sniper ammunition" id="6c10-035a-be4d-2f0f" hidden="false">
      <description>Units with weapons with this ability can select their ammo before shooting with weapons with compatible ammo ability. 
By default, executioner rounds will be used.

- Executioner round: Add 1 to that attack’s hit roll.
- Hyperfrag round: Do D3 attacks for each attack the weapon has. Reduce the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack to -1.
- Mortis round: An unmodified wound roll of 6 inflicts 1 mortal wound on the target in addition to any normal damage.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="[Action] Moving battlefield wrecks and debris." id="88ce-d161-bfbe-d554" hidden="false">
      <description>During the Movement phase any non-flying MONSTER, VEHICLE or TITANIC unit can start this action.
When doing so, that unit can push out of it&apos;s way any WRECKED VEHICLE or MONSTER, but must substract 2&quot; of it&apos;s Movement characteristic during the rest of the Phase, as it is considered to be in Difficult terrain.
TITANIC units can also push out of it&apos;s way other WRECKED TITANIC MONSTER or VEHICLE units.

INFANTRY, SWARM and BEAST units that are in the way of the pushed WRECKED unit, must be moved out of the way, moving the minimun amount possible from the original positions, while standing in unit coherency.

Non AIRCRAFT MONSTER, VEHICLE and TITANIC units in the way of the pushed WRECKED unit will stop further movement of it.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
